# Cursor Rules: RTL + Tailwind CSS

## General
- Always support `dir="rtl"` and `dir="ltr"`.
- Never use physical classes: `ml-*`, `mr-*`, `pl-*`, `pr-*`, `left-*`, `right-*`.
- Prefer logical utilities:
  - `ms-*` instead of `ml-*`
  - `me-*` instead of `mr-*`
  - `ps-*` instead of `pl-*`
  - `pe-*` instead of `pr-*`

## Layout
- Use `flex-row-reverse` only when required.
- Prefer logical alignment over manual reversing.
- Avoid hardcoded positioning (`left-0`, `right-0`).

## Text
- Use `text-start` and `text-end`.
- Avoid `text-left` and `text-right`.

## Components
- Components must work in both RTL and LTR.
- Test navigation, forms, modals, and dropdowns in RTL.

## Icons
- Mirror directional icons in RTL:
  - arrows
  - chevrons
  - breadcrumbs

## Spacing
- Use `gap-*` whenever possible.
- Prefer logical spacing over margin hacks.

## CSS
- Use logical CSS properties:
```css
margin-inline-start
margin-inline-end
padding-inline-start
padding-inline-end
inset-inline-start
inset-inline-end
text-align: start;
